# 8. AI-POWERED PURCHASE BILL UPLOAD AND DATA EXTRACTION

This feature is especially important.

Different suppliers provide purchase bills in different formats. There is no single fixed invoice layout.

The software must accept:

- PDF purchase invoices.
- Scanned PDFs.
- JPG images.
- JPEG images.
- PNG images.
- Photographs of supplier invoices.

The first version of this feature is specifically for GST purchase invoices.

Cloud AI processing is acceptable, but implement appropriate privacy safeguards and do not expose company financial data unnecessarily.

### Supplier-specific formats

The application must not assume every supplier uses the same invoice format.

It must intelligently identify the document layout and extract the relevant information.

The user must be able to define or correct what individual fields mean.

Support supplier-specific extraction rules and templates that can be reused for subsequent invoices from the same supplier.

### Information to extract

- Supplier name.
- Supplier GSTIN.
- Supplier invoice number.
- Invoice date.
- Due date, if available.
- Buyer information.
- Buyer GSTIN.
- Product name.
- Product description.
- Part number.
- HSN.
- Quantity.
- Unit.
- Rate.
- Discount.
- Taxable value.
- GST rate.
- CGST amount.
- SGST amount.
- IGST amount.
- Cess.
- Freight.
- Other charges.
- Round-off.
- Grand total.

Extract all available line-item details.

Do not ignore additional charges or tax information.

### Product matching

After extracting the invoice, match the extracted items against the existing product master.

The existing BUSY product list will be provided in Excel format.

Use the existing product master as the authoritative source for existing product names.

When a match is found, use the exact existing product name.

Do not unnecessarily create a new product because of spelling differences, abbreviations, punctuation or supplier-specific descriptions.

Matching should consider:

- Existing product name.
- OEM part number.
- Alternate part number.
- Brand.
- Manufacturer.
- SKU.
- HSN.
- Similar descriptions.

Show uncertain matches for user review.

Do not automatically merge products from different brands solely because their descriptions or part numbers appear similar.

### Purchase invoice review screen

After extraction, show an editable review screen before posting the purchase voucher.

The user must be able to:

- Correct supplier details.
- Correct invoice number and date.
- Change product mapping.
- Create a new product if necessary.
- Edit quantities.
- Edit units.
- Edit purchase rates.
- Edit discounts.
- Edit GST rates.
- Edit tax amounts where permitted.
- Edit freight and other charges.
- Correct the final invoice amount.

Show extraction confidence or warnings for uncertain fields.

Compare the calculated invoice total against the supplier's printed total.

Highlight differences.

Never post an invoice without user confirmation.

### Learning supplier formats

Save confirmed supplier-specific mapping and extraction rules.

The next time the same supplier's invoice is uploaded, reuse the saved format information.

The system should improve matching over time, but must not silently apply an uncertain mapping.

### Final posting

After approval:

- Validate the supplier.
- Validate all products.
- Validate GST calculations.
- Validate invoice totals.
- Check duplicate invoice numbers.
- Check duplicate documents.
- Create the actual purchase voucher.
- Update stock.
- Update supplier ledger.
- Update GST accounts.
- Update outstanding balances.

The entire operation must be transactional.

If posting fails, do not leave partial accounting or inventory entries.

